---
title: "112 Home Electric Power I - II"
code: "ELE-111"
category: "electrical-technology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Teaches fundamentals of residential power distribution, circuits, enclosures, protective devices, and transformers. Studies various charts and tables of the National Electrical Code. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 5 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
